toshiba-estudio2323am (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * First functionally complete release: the filter now emits a real device
    stream instead of a placeholder.

  * Protocol reversed from Windows driver captures: the 2323AM/2823AM accepts
    a standard PJL wrapper (UEL ... @PJL SET x20 ... @PJL EOJ ... UEL) carrying
    a standard ITU-T T.82 JBIG bitstream. No vendor-proprietary compression.
  * JBIG encoding via libjbig with jbg_enc_options(order=0, l0=128, mx=840,
    my=255), which reproduces the vendor BIE header byte for byte.
  * Duplex emitted as two independent fields: DUPLEX=ON|OFF plus
    BINDING=LONGEDGE|SHORTEDGE.
  * Whole-page buffering, required because IMAGELEN precedes the payload.
  * InputSlot and MediaType dropped from the PPD: the 2323AM has a single
    fixed tray and no media-type selection, so the options were dead weight.
  * PPD media sizes aligned across all four tables; A5 added.

  * Round-trip verified offline: vendor payload decodes to the expected
    4961x7016 bitmap, and our encoder output re-decodes to an identical image.
  * Package built against Debian 10 (glibc 2.28, CUPS 2.2.10) to match
    Kylin V10 SP1 (arm64) and UOS 20 (amd64).

  * Not yet validated on real hardware: acceptance of the jbigkit BIE header,
    EOJ placement in multi-page jobs, and BINDING on duplex jobs.

 -- kesat666 <keast606@gmail.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:20:00 +0800
